      "blocked_reason": "A CLEAN SIBLING-WINS AT LAST — the model hand-rolls the pipeline this tool exists to replace, and the tool's own description warns against exactly that. Surfaced 5/5, called 0/5, zero errored runs.\n\nTWO EARLIER CAUSES ARE CLOSED, which is what makes this reading trustworthy:\n  (a) THE BOOK HAD NO ONTOLOGY. Measured 5/5 before: every run went glossary_list_system_standards -> glossary_adopt_standards -> glossary_task_provide_input and never reached the tool. I filed that as sibling-wins; it was a PRECONDITION, and adopting first was correct. The seed now adopts the `character` kind, asserted BY CODE.\n  (b) THE PROMPT WITHHELD A REQUIRED INPUT. op=start 'needs source_text + model_ref'; the old prompt gave neither, on a book whose only chapter is one sentence. The prompt now carries the story, and model_ref is reachable by declaration (settings_list_models emits user_model_id, verified).\n\nWHAT REMAINS IS SELECTION, AND IT IS UNAMBIGUOUS. answerable_tools ranks this tool FIRST for its own prompt (synonym length 23, against kg_build 21). On 5 of 5 runs the model instead ran glossary_extract_entities_from_doc -> glossary_propose_entities - and SUCCEEDED at the user's goal: loreweave_glossary.glossary_entities moved 5/5. Neither of those tools is in the answerable set.\n\n🔴 AND THE TOOL SAYS SO ITSELF, in its first line: 'You do NOT pick per-entity tools: this ONE tool runs the whole pipeline - it plans WHAT to build (a worklist), builds each entity in its own focused step ..., files them as review drafts, then projects them into the graph and proposes their relationships.' The model picked per-entity tools anyway. What the author loses is not the cast - they got that - but the worklist, the deep profiles, the review drafts and the proposed relationships.\n\nSo this is P5-SIBLING-WINS arm (b): the platform already favours the right tool and the model chooses another. A description that warns against the failure did not prevent it, which bounds what documentation can fix here and is worth knowing before DQ-T41 is decided.\n\nSHIP cases stay unexercised: the tool has never completed a call.",
      "blocked_reason_updated_2026_08_24": "STILL BLOCKED — SELECTION, and the answerability layer is doing everything it can.\n\nMeasured against the deployed matcher for this exact prompt: R1 forces EXACTLY ONE tool, composition_glossary_build, via 'build the knowledge graph' (21 chars). Neither competitor is in the answerable set — glossary_extract_entities_from_doc and glossary_propose_entities declare nothing that matches this request. They are on the wire because the glossary DOMAIN is hot, not because anything judged them answerable.\n\n🔴 This corrects the numbers in the reason above ('length 23, against kg_build 21'): the match is 21, and kg_build is not in the set at all. Not a close ranking — a set of one.\n\nSo it is not a tie, not a ranking problem and not a surfacing problem. The platform favours the right tool as strongly as its design permits and the model picks the parts it can also see. The remedy the platform already has is a WORKFLOW rail — its directive says 'do NOT improvise your own tool sequence for a job a workflow already covers' — and no workflow covers this job: glossary-bootstrap is ontology setup, checked in the registry. Recorded as D-A-PIPELINE-TOOL-COMPETES-WITH-ITS-OWN-PARTS, with the recommendation left to the owner because authoring a workflow changes what every user sees in workflow_list."
